{"repositoryId":672602228,"availability":"available","full":"RafaelGB/Obsidian-ZettelFlow","name":"Obsidian-ZettelFlow","description":"Build guided Canvas workflows, read PDFs and EPUBs, and turn highlights into cited notes connected to your local Zettelkasten and knowledge graph.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":182,"forks":13,"created":"2023-07-30T16:31:05Z","updated":"2026-10-15T09:18:37Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://rafaelgb.github.io/Obsidian-ZettelFlow/","topics":["dashboard","obsidian-md","obsidian-plugin","reader","template-engine","workflow","zettelkasten","zettelkasten-methodology"],"demo":"https://rafaelgb.github.io/Obsidian-ZettelFlow/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:56.441Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:56.441Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:56.441Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T18:03:56.441Z","stars":182,"forks":13}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Practice loops · Reader & Library · Canvas workflows · Get started · Why ZettelFlow · Everything it does","Most plugins help you write. Almost none help you think.","Stop managing notes. Start managing knowledge. Obsidian is the store; ZettelFlow is the engine that makes the knowledge inside it evolve. It turns a native Canvas into a note-creation wizard, opens your notes, PDFs and EPUBs in a Reader built for thinking, and gives you a small set of practice loops that ask something of you. Every loop is offline, works with AI switched off, and writes nothing to your vault you did not decide."],"features":["ZettelFlow collects no telemetry and sends no personal data or vault contents anywhere. No account, no backend: the network is touched only by the opt-in paths below.","Everything the plugin can touch, and when","File system (vault). Reads canvas flow files and creates/edits notes (e.g. the Change note state command writes a single lifecycle property to the active note). All access goes through Obsidian's Vault /…","Vault enumeration. ZettelFlow lists every markdown file path to build the offline knowledge model that health, discovery, the graph and Cultivate all read. Paths and metadata only, all local — and you can keep folders…","Network — two opt-in paths, nothing until you use them. The community gallery does read-only GETs of the static catalog on GitHub (no backend, no account, no uploads), and the optional AI provider sends length-bounded…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RafaelGB/Obsidian-ZettelFlow/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1b9a5387b459557cf8efa08281097a26b82a24de57b0665a8d87d1b77b957026","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:56.538Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T18:03:56.538Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Practice loops · Reader & Library · Canvas workflows · Get started · Why ZettelFlow · Everything it does","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RafaelGB/Obsidian-ZettelFlow/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Stop managing notes. Start managing knowledge. Obsidian is the store; ZettelFlow is the engine that makes the knowledge inside it evolve. It turns a native Canvas into a note-creation wizard, opens your notes, PDFs and EPUBs in a Reader built for thinking, and gives you a small set of practice loops that ask something of you. Every loop is offline, works with AI switched off,…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RafaelGB/Obsidian-ZettelFlow/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No account, no backend: the network is touched only by the opt-in paths below.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/RafaelGB/Obsidian-ZettelFlow/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"optional","text":"The community gallery does read-only GETs of the static catalog on GitHub (no backend, no account, no uploads), and the optional AI provider sends length-bounded note content to the single https endpoint you configure.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Rafae